wo points", "Jackson holds a large fundraising advantage over Bottoms", "Prediction markets lean slightly Republican, around 45-47% for Bottoms"], "rationale": "The race sits at a genuine tossup: recent polls give Jackson a slim lead, most raters call it a tossup, and markets tilt modestly Republican, while the fundamentals are nearly even. A slight Republican edge of about a point best reflects the weight of evidence, with wide uncertainty given thin and mixed polling.", "watch": "Late-breaking debate dynamics, the Obama endorsement's effect on Democratic turnout, and early voting numbers could shift a margin this narrow.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Brian Kemp (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Georgia's governor race is an open-seat contest between Democrat Keisha Lance Bottoms and Republican Rick Jackson after two terms of Brian Kemp. The state leans only slightly Republican, and every major race rating through mid-October calls it a tossup, with one analyst rating it a Democratic lean.\n\nPolling since late summer shows a consistently narrow race, with most surveys giving Jackson a one-to-three point edge and a couple showing dead heats. Jackson has vastly out-raised Bottoms, though Bottoms gained a high-profile Obama endorsement in early October and the candidates met in a single televised debate focused on the economy and Trump. Markets price the race close to even with a slight Republican tilt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6414, "margin": 1.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5561, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5612, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5894, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5413, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5396, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5736, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.463, "margin": -0.7}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.5513, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_de